🔵 1. What is Django? Why is it high-level?

Django is a Python web framework that provides built-in tools like ORM, admin, authentication — that’s why it's called high-level.

🔵 2. Explain MVC. Difference with MVT.

MVC: Model, View, Controller.
MVT: Model, View, Template.
In Django the Controller is handled by the framework, so developers use MVT.

🔵 3. What are Models, Views, Templates?

Model → Database
View → Logic
Template → UI

🔵 4. Role of urls.py?

Maps URLs to views.

🟦 Virtual Environment
🔵 5. What is a virtual environment? Why use it?

Isolated environment to avoid dependency conflicts.

🔵 6. Commands for venv?

Create: python -m venv env
Activate: Win → env\Scripts\activate
Linux → source env/bin/activate

🔵 7. What if we don’t use venv?

Projects may break due to version conflicts.

🟦 Django Installation
🔵 8. Install Django?

pip install django

🔵 9. Create project?

django-admin startproject projectname

🔵 10. Create app?

python manage.py startapp appname

🔵 11. Why makemigrations and migrate?

makemigrations → prepare DB changes
migrate → apply them

🟦 URL Mapping
🔵 12. Use of path()?

Maps URL to a view.

🔵 13. Why include()?

To include app-level URL files.

🔵 14. Multiple urls.py possible?

Yes, each app can have its own.

🟦 Response / Render / Redirect
🔵 15. What is HttpResponse?

Returns plain/manual responses.

🔵 16. What is render()?

Renders an HTML template with data.

🔵 17. What is redirect()?

Redirects to another URL after actions like create/update/delete.

🟦 Templates & Static
🔵 18. Configure templates?

Add templates path in TEMPLATES['DIRS'].

🔵 19. Configure static files?

Define STATIC_URL and STATICFILES_DIRS.

🔵 20. Static files examples?

CSS, JS, images.

🟦 DTL (Django Template Language)
🔵 21. Purpose of {% extends %}?

For inheriting a base template.

🔵 22. What is {% block %}?

Defines replaceable sections.

🔵 23. What is {% include %}?

Imports reusable template components.

🔵 24. What is {% load static %}?

Allows use of static files in templates.

🔵 25. IF and FOR syntax?

{% if %}...{% endif %}
{% for i in data %}...{% endfor %}

🔵 26. What is context?

Dictionary of data passed to template.

🟦 Models, ORM & Admin
🔵 27. What is a model?

Python class representing a database table.

🔵 28. What is ORM?

Allows database operations using Python instead of SQL.

🔵 29. Create table using Django?

Define model → makemigrations → migrate.

🔵 30. Register model in admin?

admin.site.register(Model)

🔵 31. Customize admin panel?

Use ModelAdmin with list_display.

🟦 CRUD Operations
🔵 32. What is CRUD?

Create, Read, Update, Delete operations.

🔵 33. Update record using ORM?
obj = Model.objects.get(id=1)
obj.field = value
obj.save()

🔵 34. Delete record using ORM?

Model.objects.get(id=1).delete()

🟦 DRF & API
🔵 35. What is an API?

A way for two systems to communicate.

🔵 36. What is DRF? Why use it?

A Django library for building APIs quickly with serializers, authentication, etc.

🔵 37. What is a Serializer?

Converts model instances to JSON and vice versa.

🔵 38. Serializer vs ModelSerializer?

Serializer → manual fields
ModelSerializer → auto fields from model

🔵 39. What is APIView?

Class-based view for API methods like GET, POST, PUT, DELETE.

🔵 40. Use of GET, POST, PUT, DELETE?

GET → Read
POST → Create
PUT → Update
DELETE → Remove

🔵 41. What is Postman?

API testing tool.

🔵 42. Steps to create CRUD API?

Create model → serializer → views → URLs → test in Postman.

🔵 43. How to test APIs in Postman?

Choose method → enter URL → send → check response.

🔵 44. POST request failing — how to debug?

Check serializer errors, required fields, request body, and server logs.
